# libsepal valgrind suppressions.
#
# KNOWN KERNEL ARTIFACT (libcorm, not libsepal):
# corm_open() on a persistent file pushes the new handle onto a per-file id
# registry (ids_push, idm.c) that the kernel never drains in-process — 32
# bytes per file (re)open. The block is allocated and owned entirely by
# libcorm; libsepal frees everything it allocates (verified by running the
# suite with this suppression: no other leaks remain). Logged for the kernel
# maintainers; fixing it belongs to a kernel quest, not R5a.
{
   libcorm per-file id registry (corm_open -> ids_push)
   Memcheck:Leak
   match-leak-kinds: definite
   fun:malloc
   fun:ids_push
   fun:corm_open
}
